    "title": "A Nevada Bakery Has Baked The Same Sourdough Recipe Since 1980 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julian Ashford ,\n16 hours ago Forty-five years is a long time for any recipe to survive unchanged. In Nevada, a family bakery still shapes dough the same way it did back in 1980. Fresh sourdough loaves come out warm every morning, and the smell reaches the counter before you do. Cases packed with pastries, cakes,... Read full article\n2",
